<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alan II, Duke of Brittany</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 900–952</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a> · Also known as Alan Barbetorte, Alan Twisted Beard</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alan II, called Barbetorte or Twisted Beard, was a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alan-i-king-of-brittany">Alan the Great</a> who grew up in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. He returned in 936, drove the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a> out of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nantes">Nantes</a> and Brittany by 939 and ruled as duke rather than king. His restoration of Breton rule began the duchy that lasted until 1547.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alan-ii-duke-of-brittany.jpg" alt="Alan II, Duke of Brittany" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Voir description · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Entree_d%27Henri_IV_%C3%A0_Rennes_%26_Alain_Barbe-Torte.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
